{"claim_parts": ["South Africa became a republic on May 31, 1961, after a referendum held on October 5, 1960, where 52.29% of the white voters supported it", "South Africa left the British Commonwealth on the same day it declared itself a republic", "South Africa had to reapply for continued membership of the Commonwealth", "South Africa was expelled from the Commonwealth due to its apartheid policies"],
 "evidence": [{"part": 1, "relation": "entails", "same_entity": true, "same_scope": true, "quote": "The Republic of South Africa was constituted on 31 May 1961."}, {"part": 1, "relation": "entails", "same_entity": true, "same_scope": true, "quote": "A referendum on becoming a republic was held in South Africa on 5 October 1960."}, {"part": 1, "relation": "entails", "same_entity": true, "same_scope": true, "quote": "The vote, which was restricted to whites, was narrowly approved by 52.29% of the voters."}, {"part": 2, "relation": "entails", "same_entity": true, "same_scope": true, "quote": "South Africa withdrew from the Commonwealth on 31 May 1961, the day that the Republic came into existence."}, {"part": 3, "relation": "entails", "same_entity": true, "same_scope": true, "quote": "South Africa needed to reapply for continued membership of the Commonwealth"}, {"part": 4, "relation": "contradicts", "same_entity": true, "same_scope": true, "quote": "As a result, South Africa withdrew from the Commonwealth on 31 May 1961"}, {"part": 4, "relation": "insufficient", "same_entity": true, "same_scope": false, "quote": "they would go to any lengths to expel South Africa from the Commonwealth"}, {"part": 4, "relation": "insufficient", "same_entity": true, "same_scope": false, "quote": "it became clear that African and Asian member states would oppose South Africa due to its apartheid policies"}],
 "missing_conditions": []}

{"claim_parts": ["The casualties of support personnel recruited from outside Europe, which were not included previously, have been revised in recent research.", "Comparing casualty figures from different sources is not uniform and cannot be considered comparable in all cases."],
"evidence": [{"part": 1, "relation": "entails", "same_entity": true, "same_scope": true, "quote": "they include in their listing of military war dead personnel outside of combat theaters and civilians recruited from Africa, the Middle East and China who provided logistical and service support in combat theaters"}, {"part": 1, "relation": "entails", "same_entity": true, "same_scope": true, "quote": "The casualties of these support personnel recruited outside of Europe were previously not included with British war dead"}, {"part": 2, "relation": "entails", "same_entity": true, "same_scope": true, "quote": "The methodology used by each nation to record and classify casualties was not uniform, a general caveat regarding casualty figures is that they cannot be considered comparable in all cases"}],
"missing_conditions": [{"part": 1, "text": "The revision is specifically research by the Commonwealth War Graves Commission that revised the military casualty statistics of the UK and its allies, not revisions in general.", "quote": "More recently the research of the Commonwealth War Graves Commission (CWGC) has revised the military casualty statistics of the UK and its allies"}]}

{"claim_parts": ["The term \"mellitus\" was added by the Briton John Rolle", "The term \"mellitus\" was added in the late 1700s", "The term \"mellitus\" was added to separate the condition from diabetes insipidus"],
"evidence": [{"part": 1, "relation": "entails", "same_entity": true, "same_scope": true, "quote": "The term \"mellitus\" or \"from honey\" was added by the Briton John Rolle in the late 1700s to separate the condition from diabetes insipidus, which is also associated with frequent urination."}, {"part": 2, "relation": "entails", "same_entity": true, "same_scope": true, "quote": "The term \"mellitus\" or \"from honey\" was added by the Briton John Rolle in the late 1700s to separate the condition from diabetes insipidus, which is also associated with frequent urination."}, {"part": 3, "relation": "entails", "same_entity": true, "same_scope": true, "quote": "The term \"mellitus\" or \"from honey\" was added by the Briton John Rolle in the late 1700s to separate the condition from diabetes insipidus, which is also associated with frequent urination."}],
"missing_conditions": []}

{"claim_parts": ["The 2017 Arkane \"Prey\" is considered a reimagining of the intellectual property.", "The 2017 Arkane \"Prey\" is not related to the planned sequel."],
"evidence": [{"part": 1, "relation": "entails", "same_entity": true, "same_scope": true, "quote": "is considered a reimagining of the intellectual property set in a wholly new narrative"}, {"part": 2, "relation": "insufficient", "same_entity": true, "same_scope": false, "quote": "Arkane's game does not use any of the planned sequel's assets"}, {"part": 2, "relation": "insufficient", "same_entity": false, "same_scope": false, "quote": "is largely unrelated to the 2006 game"}],
"missing_conditions": [{"part": 2, "text": "The source says Arkane's game does not use the planned sequel's assets, but it only incorporates the previous game's name and broad theme, so it is not wholly unrelated to the franchise. The claim's unqualified 'not related' omits this.", "quote": "only incorporates the previous game's name and the broad theme of the protagonist being hunted by aliens"}]}
